- ℹ️ `src/App.tsx:301` - This edge case is in the round-1 fix for settle-errors-swallowed. `settleFromChat` now re-reads the summary in a `finally` block with `setReviews(await host.reviewSummary())`. If that re-read rejects, its error takes the place of the settle&#39;s own outcome. So when every `reviewSettle` succeeds but the summary read fails, the card still shows &#34;That did not settle: ...&#34;, which is wrong because the threads were settled. And when both calls fail, the captain sees the summary&#39;s error instead of the settle&#39;s. Fix: catch the summary re-read on its own (for example `await host.reviewSummary().then(setReviews, () =&gt; {})`, or put its error in a separate message), so the settle outcome is what the card reports.

🔧 Fix applied.
✅ Re-checked - no issues remain.
