<details>
<summary>🔧 **Test** - 2 issues found → auto-fixed ✅</summary>

- ⚠️ `src-tauri/src/review-frame.js:550` - The picture snapdom draws uses fallback fonts, not the page&#39;s own. snapdom fetches the page&#39;s @font-face files with credentials &#39;include&#39;, because the frame&#39;s location.origin matches the font URL even though the sandboxed document&#39;s origin is &#39;null&#39;. The server answers with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, and browsers reject a wildcard on a credentialed request, so the fetch fails. The console says: &#34;must not be the wildcard &#39;*&#39; when the request&#39;s credentials mode is &#39;include&#39;&#34;. The picture still draws and outlines the right place (`picture-wildcard.jpg` next to `page-region-wildcard.png`), but its text is in fallback fonts. `artifact.rs` sends the same wildcard, so the packaged app very likely behaves the same way; I did not verify that in the packaged app. Possible fixes: have the frame script tell snapdom to fetch without credentials, or answer these requests with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: null` plus `Allow-Credentials`.
- ℹ️ `vite.config.ts:28` - Fixed a gap in the test harness: the Vite mock served fixture files other than HTML without `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. The app&#39;s scheme sends that header on every artifact file, so in the mock the new usage-panel fixture&#39;s fonts were blocked in the sandboxed frame and the page rendered differently from the app. The mock now adds the header to every `/artifacts/` response. `pnpm artifacts` still passes all 238 checks after the change.
